\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Thou before whose presence
\par Nought evil may come in,
\par Yet who dost look in mercy
\par Down on this world of sin;
\par O give us noble purpose
\par To set the sin- bound free,
\par And Christ- like tender pity
\par To seek the lost for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our foe is fierce and subtle;
\par The forces at his hand,
\par With woes that none can number,
\par Despoil the pleasant land:
\par All they who  war against them,
\par In strife so keen and long,
\par Must in their Saviour's armour
\par Be stronger than the strong.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. 'Tis Thou hast wrought among us
\par The great things that we see:
\par For things that are we thank Thee,
\par And for the things to be;
\par For bright hope that confirmeth
\par Faint hands and feeble knees
\par To strive beneath Thy blessing
\par For greater things than these.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lead on, O Love and Mercy,
\par O Purity ans Power!
\par Lead on till peace eternal
\par Shall close this battle- hour;
\par Till all who prayed and struggled
\par To set their brethren free,
\par In triumph meet to praise Thee,
\par Most Holy Trinity.
\par                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

